  "full_response": "Certainly! Below is a sample Terraform variables file named `variables.tf` that includes placeholders for your Azure subscription ID, client secret, tenant ID, and storage account access key.\n\n```hcl\nvariable \"subscription_id\" {\n  description = \"The Azure Subscription ID\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n\nvariable \"client_secret\" {\n  description = \"The Azure Secret\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n\nvariable \"tenant_id\" {\n  description = \"The Azure Tenant ID\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n\nvariable \"storage_account_access_key\" {\n  description = \"The access key for the Azure Storage Account\"\n  type        = string\n  sensitive   = true\n}\n```\n\nSave this file as `variables.tf` in your Terraform configuration directory. When you run `terraform plan` or `terraform apply`, you will need to provide values for these variables, potentially via environment variables, a `.tfvars` file, or a CLI input file.\n\nMake sure you handle these sensitive variables securely, especially by avoiding storing them in plaintext or leaving them in version control.",
